<title>USA: Arthur Andersen appoints Jim Wadia to top post-WSJ.</title>
<headline>Arthur Andersen appoints Jim Wadia to top post-WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Arthur Andersen appointed Jim Wadia to succeed Richard Measelle as its world-wide managing partner, The Wall Street Journal said.</p>
<p>In Wednesday's electronic edition, the paper said Wadia won the top post at the the giant accounting firm after losing a battle to become managing partner and chief executive of Andersen Worldwide, the parent of Arthur Andersen.</p>
<p>Wadia has been with Andersen since 1977, the paper said.</p>
